CAT = "accafaConsolidation"; SEG = "CON"
def m(v): return "${:,.0f}".format(v)
_cons = 640000 + 120000 * 2.40
Q = [
("A subsidiary is an entity that is:",
 "Controlled by another entity", ["Significantly influenced by another", "Owned 20% to 50% by one investor", "Jointly controlled by two investors"],
 "Under IFRS 10, a parent consolidates the entities it controls. Significant influence, usually 20% to 50% of the votes, gives an associate."),
("An investor controls an investee when it has power over it, exposure to variable returns from it and:",
 "The ability to use its power to affect those returns", ["Ownership of all of its shares", "A seat on its audit committee", "The investee's consent to consolidation"],
 "IFRS 10 requires all three elements. Control can exist with less than 100%, or even less than 50%, of the shares."),
("P owns 45% of S's voting shares. Under an agreement with other shareholders, P can appoint most of S's board. S is:",
 "A subsidiary of P", ["An associate of P", "A trade investment of P", "Unrelated to P"],
 "Control does not depend on holding over half the shares. The power to appoint a majority of the board gives P control, so S is consolidated."),
("P bought 80% of S for $640,000 cash plus 120,000 of its own shares with a fair value of $2.40 each. The non-controlling interest's fair value was $230,000. S's net assets had a carrying amount of $845,000, and its land was worth $55,000 more than its carrying amount. Goodwill is:",
 m(_cons + 230000 - 900000), [m(640000 + 120000 + 230000 - 900000), m(_cons - 900000), m(_cons + 230000 - 845000)],
 "Consideration is $640,000 + $288,000 = $928,000. Goodwill = $928,000 + $230,000 - ($845,000 + $55,000) = $258,000. Valuing the shares at $1 each would give $90,000."),
("At acquisition, the non-controlling interest (20%) in S was measured at its fair value of $230,000. S has made post-acquisition profits of $135,000. The non-controlling interest in the consolidated statement of financial position is:",
 m(230000 + 0.2 * 135000), [m(230000), m(230000 + 135000), m(230000 - 0.2 * 135000)],
 "NCI = fair value at acquisition + NCI share of post-acquisition profits = $230,000 + 20% x $135,000 = $257,000."),
("P's receivables are $84,000 and S's are $57,000. S's receivables include $6,500 owed by P, and the current accounts agree. Consolidated receivables are:",
 m(84000 + 57000 - 6500), [m(84000 + 57000), m(84000 + 57000 - 2 * 6500), m(84000 + 57000 + 6500)],
 "Intra-group balances are cancelled: $84,000 + $57,000 - $6,500 = $134,500. P's matching $6,500 payable is removed from consolidated payables."),
("P sold goods to S for $36,000 at a mark-up of 20% on cost. A quarter of the goods are still in S's inventory at the year end. The unrealised profit to remove is:",
 m(36000 / 4 * 20 / 120), [m(36000 / 4 * 0.20), m(36000 * 20 / 120), m(36000 / 4)],
 "Goods still held cost S $9,000. Profit within them at a 20% mark-up is $9,000 x 20/120 = $1,500. Taking 20% of $9,000 treats the mark-up as a margin."),
("P sold goods to its subsidiary S at a profit, and some are still in S's inventory. The unrealised profit is removed from:",
 "Group retained earnings and inventory", ["NCI and inventory", "Group revenue only", "Goodwill and inventory"],
 "Because the parent was the seller, the profit sits in the parent's retained earnings. It is removed from there and from inventory, and the NCI is not affected."),
("P's revenue is $960,000 and S's is $540,000. During the year S sold goods for $75,000 to P. Consolidated revenue is:",
 m(960000 + 540000 - 75000), [m(960000 + 540000), m(960000 + 540000 - 2 * 75000), m(960000 + 540000 - 35000)],
 "The group cannot sell to itself, so intra-group sales are removed: $960,000 + $540,000 - $75,000 = $1,425,000. The same amount is removed from cost of sales."),
("P acquired S on 1 October. The year end is 31 December. S's revenue for the year was $480,000, earned evenly. The amount of S's revenue in the consolidated statement of profit or loss is:",
 m(480000 * 3 / 12), [m(480000), m(480000 * 9 / 12), m(480000 / 12)],
 "Only results after acquisition are consolidated: three months, $480,000 x 3/12 = $120,000. The first nine months were earned before P owned S."),
("At acquisition, S's land had a carrying amount of $300,000 and a fair value of $385,000. In the consolidated statement of financial position the land is included at:",
 m(385000), [m(300000), m(385000 - 300000), m(300000 + 385000)],
 "S's assets are consolidated at their fair value at acquisition. The $85,000 increase also raises S's net assets at acquisition in the goodwill calculation."),
("P issued 400,000 $1 shares, with a market value of $2.75 each, to acquire S. In the goodwill calculation, this consideration is measured at:",
 m(400000 * 2.75), [m(400000), m(400000 * 1.75), m(400000 * 3.75)],
 "Consideration is measured at fair value: 400,000 x $2.75 = $1,100,000. In P's own books this is $400,000 share capital and $700,000 share premium."),
("An investor holds 30% of a company's voting shares and has significant influence but not control. It accounts for the company as:",
 "An associate, by the equity method", ["A subsidiary, by consolidation", "A trade investment, at cost only", "An associate, line by line"],
 "An associate is not consolidated line by line. The investment is shown as one line, at cost plus the investor's share of post-acquisition profits."),
("An investor paid $180,000 for 25% of an associate. Since then the associate has made profits of $64,000. Under the equity method, the investment is carried at:",
 m(180000 + 0.25 * 64000), [m(180000 + 64000), m(180000), m(180000 - 0.25 * 64000)],
 "Investment = cost + share of post-acquisition profits = $180,000 + 25% x $64,000 = $196,000."),
("Which of these usually indicates that an investor has significant influence over a company?",
 "Representation on its board", ["Owning 8% of its shares, no seat", "Holding only non-voting shares", "Being one of many customers"],
 "IAS 28 lists board representation, taking part in policy decisions, material transactions and key staff interchange as indicators. A small, passive holding gives no influence."),
("P holds 6% of Q's shares and has no influence over Q's policies. In P's financial statements, Q is:",
 "A trade (simple) investment", ["An associate", "A subsidiary", "A joint arrangement"],
 "Without control or significant influence the holding is a simple investment, shown as an asset, not consolidated or equity accounted."),
]
